@* Terms and Conditions in English. The Bulgarian version is Terms.cshtml: a change goes into both files. *@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms and Conditions";
}

<article class="tg-legal">
    <header class="tg-page-head">
        <div>
            <h1 class="tg-page-head__title">Terms and Conditions</h1>
            <p class="tg-page-head__sub">Last updated: 01.11.2026</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>The website tournamentgalaxy.bg ("Tournament Galaxy", "the platform") is run by:</p>
        <partial name="_LegalOperator" />
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>2. What we offer</h2>
        <p>
            Tournament Galaxy is a platform for amateur football tournaments: cities and tournaments, team registration for
            a participation fee, referees, results, rankings and pictures from the tournaments. These terms govern the use
            of the website and taking part in the tournaments. You accept them when you register and every time you enter
            a tournament.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>3. Account</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Accounts can be created by persons aged 18 or over, with a real e-mail address that you confirm.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for your password and for what is done from your account.</li>
            <li>You can delete your account at any time in "My Profile". What is kept afterwards is described in the <a asp-action="Privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Coaches and teams</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>A coach enters a team of 6 to 10 players. A coach can take part in only one active tournament at a time.</li>
            <li>
                When entering a tournament, the coach confirms that the players know about it and agree to take part (for
                players under 18, their parents or guardians agree as well), that to the best of the coach's knowledge the
                players are in good health, and that the team will follow the rules.
            </li>
            <li>The players' names are not shown publicly.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>5. Participation fee and payment</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>The participation fee is shown with each tournament, in euro, and is the final price.</li>
            <li>Payment is made by card through Stripe. Card details are entered directly at Stripe and never reach us.</li>
            <li>The team is entered right after the payment succeeds, and you get a notification.</li>
            <li>If the tournament fills up or starts while you are paying, the amount is refunded automatically.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>6. Right of withdrawal and refunds</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                Taking part in a tournament is a leisure service on a specific date. The statutory 14-day right of
                withdrawal from distance contracts therefore does not apply.
            </li>
            <li>
                You can leave a tournament until it starts ("Participations → As coach"), but the fee is not refunded
                automatically. You can write to us and ask for a refund.
            </li>
            <li>
                The fee is refunded in full and automatically to the card it was paid with when: the organisers cancel the
                tournament before it starts; fewer than 8 teams are entered when it is due to start and it is cancelled
                automatically; the payment went through but the team could not be entered.
            </li>
            <li>
                If the organisers change the date of a tournament, you will be notified. If you cannot take part on the new
                date, write to us before the start and we will refund the fee.
            </li>
            <li>How long a refund takes to appear on the card depends on the bank (usually 5–10 working days).</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>7. How the tournaments run</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Tournaments are played as knockouts; every match has a winner.</li>
            <li>Teams follow the tournament rules and the instructions of the organisers and referees. The results are entered by the organisers.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>8. Prizes</h2>
        <p>
            The prize money is shown with each tournament. After the final, the organisers contact the coaches of the teams
            in the top three places to pay out the prizes. Prizes are taxed as the law requires.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>9. Referees, ratings and comments</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Persons aged 18 or over with at least 2 years of experience can become referees.</li>
            <li>Users can rate referees and comment on them. Comments must be relevant and respectful.</li>
            <li>
                Insults, defamation, threats, discriminatory content, advertising, other people's personal data (for example
                phone numbers and addresses) and anything else that is illegal are not allowed.
            </li>
            <li>
                Anybody can report a comment with the "Report" button below it. The organisers review the reports and remove
                comments that break these rules; the author gets a notification with the reason.
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>10. Pictures</h2>
        <p>
            The organisers may publish pictures from the tournaments in the website's gallery. If you are in a picture and
            want it taken down, write to us and we will remove it. We remove a picture of a child at a parent's request.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>11. Liability</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Taking part is at your own risk, as described in the declaration when entering a tournament.</li>
            <li>
                The organisers are not liable for damage unless it was caused intentionally or by gross negligence, or where
                the law does not allow liability to be limited.
            </li>
            <li>We are not liable for the website being temporarily unavailable because of maintenance or technical problems.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>12. Complaints and disputes</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Send complaints and questions through "Contact the organisers" in your profile or to the e-mail address above. We answer within 14 days.</li>
            <li>
                If we cannot agree, you can turn to the Bulgarian Commission for Consumer Protection
                (<a href="https://kzp.bg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kzp.bg</a>) and its general conciliation committees
                for out-of-court settlement of the dispute.
            </li>
            <li>Bulgarian law applies. Disputes are settled by the competent Bulgarian court.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>13. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
            We may change these terms. We will notify you on the website of important changes. Changes do not affect
            registrations that have already been paid.
        </p>
    </section>
</article>
